"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2694,"**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Abu Bakr al-Hanafi, narrated to us 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said:
""Ihram was once made from Dhu'l-Hulayfah from near the tree, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he came to Dhu Tawa, spent the night there until he prayed the dawn prayer, then performed ghusl (ritual bath). Then he entered Makkah from the upper side from Kudā, and exited when he exited from Kudā from the lower side of Makkah."""
2695,"**
Narrated to us Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad, who said: My father narrated to me, on the authority of his father, from Ayyub, from Nafi', that Ibn 'Umar (RA) would, when he reached Dhu al-Hulayfah, command that his camel be made ready, then he would pray the dawn prayer, then ride until it stood upright with him. He would then face the qiblah and recite the talbiyah, continuing to do so until he reached the Haram. Upon reaching Dhu Twa, he would spend the night there. He said: He would pray the dawn prayer there, then perform ghusl (ritual bath), and he claimed that the Prophet (ﷺ) did likewise."
